  "full_text": "So the Christian Bible is pretty clear on unevenly yoked families and stuff and saving your children and all that. I saw a family where I kind of condemned the one and not the other spouse. I don't know what you do with the kids, man. Well, do I have to? Because I don't know. You could say don't kill kids, I guess. You have to look at the impact on the heart of the military. What are we going to do to them? I think we want to feel safe, I don't know. After the Napoleonic War, the British monarch sent, no, after the War of 1812, well. We won the war of 1812, and the British invaded like two weeks after the war. And there's a YouTube video, and it makes very clear that the British were trying to get rid of the Napoleonic soldiers. And anyway, it's pretty harsh. But I got to thinking, what if they were just monsters or something? I mean, you can't tolerate that, I guess. I don't know. But that's what that monarch decided. You know, after the French Revolution, you know, there's a threat to the monarchy. Anyway, so like, oh well.",
